ALERT: Agents must read `AGENT=1 cron-person skill` before using this tool.
command: cron-person task
summary: Inspect and trigger scheduled tasks
description: Commands for listing, manually triggering, and reviewing the run history of individual tasks.
usage: cron-person task [flags] [command]
subcommands:
  - history [dir]: List recent task runs, newest first
  - list: List all tasks defined across all authorized directories
  - log <run-id>: Show the details and captured output of a task run
  - run <dir> <command...>: Manually execute a task inside a target directory
flags:
  --config string: Path to custom configuration file (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
  -h, --help bool: help for task
  --store string: Path to custom authorization state file (default: $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)
